    "description": "Side quest parallel to 4.1 (does not wait on Forth 2012 Core).\n\nQuestion: can NanoISA become rich enough in syntax/metadata to be turned back\ninto almost any high-level language \u2014 not \"can I dump bytecode into a C\ninterpreter.\"\n\nRoadmap items (docs/ROADMAP.md):\n1. Write docs/NANOISA_HL_ROUNDTRIP.md with the reconstruction contract.\n2. Inventory .nvm v2 sections vs reconstruction needs (local names are slots).\n3. Pin a small --emit-nvm fixture and record recoverability without source.\n4. Spike two HLL surfaces from the same .nvm (structured C + NanoLang or other).\n   Fail if either is only a VM embedded in that language. No product nvm2c.\n5. Publish sufficient / insufficient / blocked-on-named-metadata. Do not delete\n   transpiler.nano. Do not claim Core. Do not claim any target language.\n\nCanonical disassembly round-trip is a different test (bytecode, not HLL).\n",
